--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,43 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkey management
+
+Account settings are at `/devtools-times/account/settings`. Login now goes through
+an Astro endpoint, which retains the upstream bearer token in the server session
+rather than exposing it to browser storage. The account service must return
+`{ "token": "..." }` from `POST /login`.
+
+Set the server environment variable `ACCOUNT_API_URL` to your existing account
+service's API root (without a trailing slash). It defaults to the legacy Times
+API used by the sign-in form. **That legacy service does not currently expose the
+credential endpoints below; deployment needs a compatible backend.** The UI
+reports service unavailability until that backend is configured. No sample
+credentials are created, and a service error is never treated as an empty list.
+
+Required authenticated backend contract (all credential routes receive
+`Authorization: Bearer <token>`):
+
+- `GET /credentials`: return the complete, unpaginated authoritative list as
+  `{ rpId, userId, credentials: [{ id, name, provider?, registeredAt, lastUsedAt? }] }`.
+  `userId` is the original WebAuthn user handle encoded as base64url; each `id`
+  is the original base64url credential ID. `rpId` must match registration and the
+  deployed domain. Dates are epoch **milliseconds**, with `lastUsedAt` nullable.
+  `provider` may be populated from AAGUID metadata during registration; it is a
+  display hint only. Never return a partial list: browser sync may remove omitted
+  credentials from the authenticator.
+- `PUT /credential/:id`: accept `{ name }` (1–100 characters after trimming),
+  persist the nickname, and return a successful HTTP status.
+- `DELETE /credential/:id`: revoke the credential and return a successful HTTP
+  status. Enforce any account recovery / last sign-in method policy here.
+- Every route must validate the token and restrict reads and writes to that
+  token's account. Return 401 for expired tokens; enforce ownership, validation,
+  and durable account-wide persistence in the service. Credential registration
+  and authentication remain the responsibility of that service.
+
+On settings load and after successful deletion, the client reloads the complete
+list and feature-detects `PublicKeyCredential.signalAllAcceptedCredentials`.
+Unsupported browsers and failed signals show manual password-manager guidance.
+Nickname changes affect the account's key label only; they do not change the
+WebAuthn account profile or invoke `signalCurrentUserDetails`.
